
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>CSS Pseudo-Classes Explained</title>
<style>
body{font-family:Arial;margin:0;padding:20px;background:#f1f5f9;color:#1e293b}
section{max-width:900px;margin:20px auto;padding:20px;background:white;border-radius:8px}
.demo{padding:12px;margin:8px 0;background:#dbeafe;border-radius:5px}
.demo:hover{background:#bfdbfe}
button{padding:10px 15px;border:0;border-radius:5px;background:#2563eb;color:white;cursor:pointer}
button:hover{background:#1e40af}
input{padding:10px;border:1px solid #94a3b8;border-radius:5px}
input:focus{outline:3px solid #93c5fd;border-color:#2563eb}
li:first-child{color:#047857;font-weight:bold}
li:last-child{color:#be123c}
tr:nth-child(even){background:#eff6ff}
a:visited{color:#7c3aed}
a:active{color:#dc2626}
.box:checked+label{color:#047857;font-weight:bold}
table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%}
td,th{border:1px solid #cbd5e1;padding:9px;text-align:left}
th{background:#dbeafe}
code{color:#9a3412}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<section>
<h1>CSS Pseudo-Classes</h1>
<p><b>Definition:</b> A pseudo-class selects an element in a special state.</p>
<p><code>selector:pseudo-class { property: value; }</code></p>
</section>
<section>
<h2>1. :hover</h2><p>Move your mouse over the box.</p>
<div class="demo">Hover over me</div>
<h2>2. :focus</h2><p>Click inside the input field.</p>
<input placeholder="Click here to test focus">
<h2>3. :active</h2><p>Press and hold the button.</p>
<button>Press me</button>
<h2>4. :first-child and :last-child</h2>
<ul><li>First item</li><li>Middle item</li><li>Last item</li></ul>
<h2>5. :nth-child(even)</h2>
<table><tr><th>Name</th><th>Marks</th></tr><tr><td>Aman</td><td>80</td></tr><tr><td>Riya</td><td>90</td></tr><tr><td>Raj</td><td>75</td></tr><tr><td>Neha</td><td>88</td></tr></table>
<h2>6. :checked</h2>
<input class="box" type="checkbox" id="agree"><label for="agree"> Tick this checkbox</label>
<h2>7. :disabled and :enabled</h2>
<input placeholder="Enabled input">
<input placeholder="Disabled input" disabled>
<h2>8. :required and :optional</h2>
<input required placeholder="Required field">
<input placeholder="Optional field">
<h2>9. :not()</h2>
<p>Example selector: <code>p:not(.special)</code> selects paragraphs without class="special".</p>
<h2>10. :empty</h2>
<p>Example selector: <code>div:empty</code> selects elements that have no child nodes.</p>
</section>
<section>
<h2>Quick Reference Table</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>Pseudo-class</th><th>Simple explanation</th></tr>
<tr><td>:hover</td><td>When the pointer is over an element.</td></tr>
<tr><td>:focus</td><td>When an element has focus.</td></tr>
<tr><td>:active</td><td>While an element is being activated.</td></tr>
<tr><td>:visited</td><td>For a visited link.</td></tr>
<tr><td>:first-child</td><td>When the element is the first child.</td></tr>
<tr><td>:last-child</td><td>When the element is the last child.</td></tr>
<tr><td>:nth-child()</td><td>Selects children by position or pattern.</td></tr>
<tr><td>:checked</td><td>For a checked checkbox or radio button.</td></tr>
<tr><td>:disabled</td><td>For a disabled form control.</td></tr>
<tr><td>:enabled</td><td>For an enabled form control.</td></tr>
<tr><td>:required</td><td>For a required form field.</td></tr>
<tr><td>:optional</td><td>For a field that is not required.</td></tr>
<tr><td>:not()</td><td>Selects elements that do not match a selector.</td></tr>
<tr><td>:empty</td><td>Selects elements with no child nodes.</td></tr>
</table>
</section>
</body>
</html>
